### Flutter Map Camera Constraint Configuration

Source: https://context7.com/fleaflet/flutter_map/llms.txt

Constrains the map view to specific geographic bounds using flutter_map. It defines bounds (e.g., Europe) and applies them to `CameraConstraint.contain` or `CameraConstraint.containCenter`. The `TileLayer` can also be constrained to these bounds.

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';
import 'package:flutter_map/flutter_map.dart';
import 'package:latlong2/latlong.dart';

class CameraConstraintExample extends StatelessWidget {
  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    // Define bounds (e.g., constrain to Europe)
    final europeBounds = LatLngBounds(
      LatLng(35.0, -10.0),  // Southwest
      LatLng(71.0, 40.0),   // Northeast
    );

    return Scaffold(
      body: FlutterMap(
        options: MapOptions(
          initialCenter: LatLng(51.5, -0.09),
          initialZoom: 5.0,
          // Constrain entire map to stay within bounds
          cameraConstraint: CameraConstraint.contain(
            bounds: europeBounds,
          ),
          // Alternative: constrain only center point
          // cameraConstraint: CameraConstraint.containCenter(
          //   bounds: europeBounds,
          // ),
        ),
        children: [
          TileLayer(
            urlTemplate: 'https://tile.openstreetmap.org/{z}/{x}/{y}.png',
            userAgentPackageName: 'com.example.app',
            // Optionally constrain tile loading to bounds
            tileBounds: europeBounds,
          ),
        ],
      ),
    );
  }
}

```

